  "functions": [
    {
      "id": "unit-cell-size",
      "name": "UnitCellSize",
      "category": "SweepingMeshSDF",
      "signature": "UnitCellSize()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "CellSizeType",
      "docs": "Compute discretely-sampled (ie gridded) signed distance field for a mesh\nThe basic approach is, first compute exact Distances in a narrow band, and then\nextend out to rest of Grid using fast \"sweeping\" (ie like a distance transform).\nThe resulting unsigned Grid is then signed using ray-intersection counting, which\nis also computed on the Grid, so no BVH is necessary\nIf you set ComputeMode to NarrowBandOnly, result is a narrow-band signed distance field.\nThis is quite a bit faster as the sweeping is the most computationally-intensive step.\nYou can optionally provide a spatial data structure to allow faster computation of\nnarrow-band Distances; this is most beneficial if we want a wider band\nCaveats:\n- the \"narrow band\" is based on triangle bounding boxes, so it is not necessarily\nthat \"narrow\" if you have large triangles on a diagonal to Grid axes\nTODO: a number of utility function could & should be shared between this and CachingMeshSDF!\nThis code is based on the implementation found at https://github.com/christopherbatty/SDFGen"
    },
    {
      "id": "set-cell-size",
      "name": "SetCellSize",
      "category": "SweepingMeshSDF",
      "signature": "SetCellSize(Target, In Cell Size)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TSweepingMeshSDF*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Cell Size",
          "type": "Float"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void"
    },
